+
+- Flash Next on CUDA: the routing width and the shared expert's width come from the checkpoint's `config.json` (`num_experts_per_tok`, `shared_expert_intermediate_size`): top-10 with a 640-wide shared expert as before, or top-5 with a 1280-wide one; any other value is refused by the field's name, as is a captured kernel set with the top-5 shape (#3368).
+
 ## 1.2.9
 
 - Flash Next on CUDA: a lone stream draws on its own path again; the batched draws #2927 added now run only when two or more streams share a step, so one sampled stream no longer pays the group's whole-buffer download each step. Tokens are unchanged (#3391, after #2927).
